#N canvas 100 100 700 560 10;
#X obj 40 40 jet_win;
#X msg 40 80 create;
#X msg 130 80 destroy;
#X obj 40 130 jet_head 0;
#X obj 40 165 jet_color 0.9 0.3 0.5;
#X obj 40 200 jet_ellipse 3 1.5;
#X floatatom 40 250 5 0 5 0 - - -;
#X floatatom 130 250 5 0 5 0 - - -;
#X text 40 275 radius x;
#X text 130 275 radius y;
#X msg 240 250 size 3 1;
#X msg 320 250 size 1 3;
#X msg 400 250 size 2;
#X text 40 320 [jet_ellipse rx ry] is a filled ellipse with a smooth edge (see jet_circle for how). rx and ry are the two half axes in Gem units - [jet_ellipse 3 1.5] is 6 units wide and 3 tall. One argument makes a circle. It is centred on the origin of the chain: move it with jet_translateXYZ\, tilt it with jet_rotateXYZ (it is real 3D\, so tilting around X or Y foreshortens it in perspective).;
#X text 40 440 Inlets\: the chain (bang \, plus "size rx ry" or "size r")\, radius x\, radius y. The radius inlets only store - drawing happens on the next bang. Colour from jet_color\, a current texture is shown inside the ellipse. The bang is forwarded.;
#X connect 1 0 0 0;
#X connect 2 0 0 0;
#X connect 3 0 4 0;
#X connect 4 0 5 0;
#X connect 6 0 5 1;
#X connect 7 0 5 2;
#X connect 10 0 5 0;
#X connect 11 0 5 0;
#X connect 12 0 5 0;
